**How to implement.** The table's elements ARE the active setup's slots: one record, not two of the same shape (001 §J 'The table draws the active setup'; the S8.2 brief: 'slots map to table elements … Placing an element binds a slot'; AGENTS.md 'A bijection is collapsed, not bridged … the LOWER type survives'). `TableAndElementRotationView`'s `TestElement` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:TestElement`, `{ id; placement; zoom; beam }`) is the shape of `Setups.SetupSlot` (step 256) without its content, and `SetupSlot` is the lower type (Domain), so `TestElement` is deleted. Nothing about what is drawn, laid out or run changes in this step. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (a) `TestElement` is deleted, and `TableAndElementRotationModel.elements` becomes `Setups.SetupSlot list`, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2: the table's slots, the light source (the ray root) first. (b) `TestElement`'s members `elementX` and `boxCorners` move unchanged onto a `type Setups.SetupSlot with` extension at the same place in the file, and the `type TestElement with` extension further down (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, the one holding the drawing members) becomes `type Setups.SetupSlot with`. (c) `mkElement`, `mainSeedElements` and `initInverse`'s three seeds (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:mkElement`, `:mainSeedElements`, `:initInverse`), and every other record that built a `TestElement`, build a `SetupSlot` with `content = Setups.EmptySlotContent`: `AddElement`, `AddElementBoundTo` and `PlaceOnBeam` place a slot of the table, empty until step 263 puts an item in it. (d) `model.layoutElements` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:layoutElements`) is `model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.layoutElement)` (step 256), its hand-written record deleted. (e) `captureScene` and `restoreScene` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:captureScene`, `:restoreScene`) map a `SetupSlot` to a `Scene.SceneElement` and back with `EmptySlotContent`, until step 260 deletes all three. (f) Every `TestElement` annotation in the file names `Setups.SetupSlot`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/ElementRotationView.fs`: its `TestElement` annotations name `Setups.SetupSlot` and `initElementRotation`'s `onRay` builds one with `content = Setups.EmptySlotContent`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`: the doc of `SceneElement` that names `TestElement` names `SetupSlot` instead, in no more words. (4) Tests, their assertions unchanged: every `TestElement` annotation or record in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs` and in the UI suite's `ElementMenuTests.fs`, `ElementRotationTests.fs`, `ExperimentControlsTests.fs`, `InverseConstructorTests.fs`, `LayerBandsControlsTests.fs`, `LibraryControlsTests.fs`, `MainSceneMsgTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`, `SourceAndDetectorMoveTests.fs`, `TableAndElementRotationTests.fs` and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs` names `Setups.SetupSlot` (or `SetupSlot` under an `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups`), and a record of one gains `content = EmptySlotContent` (`OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`' flagged sample, `SceneRoundTripTests.fs`' three fixture elements). The other readers of the model's elements in the census, `OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs` and the UI suite's `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`, `LibraryWindowTests.fs`, `LightSourceEditorTests.fs` and `ScrollExtentTests.fs`, compile over `SetupSlot` as they are; a record of an element they build gains the content, and nothing else changes in them. `MainSceneMsgTests` gains `the table's elements are slots: each one placed is empty, and each lays out as the table lays it out`: every element of `initMain ()` holds `EmptySlotContent`; after `AddElement LinearPolarizer` and `AddElement Sample` the new elements do too; and `model.layoutElements` equals `model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.layoutElement)`. No other type, member or behaviour changes. After this step `git grep -n -w "TestElement" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the table's elements become slots, `TestElement` MUST be gone, `TableAndElementRotationModel.elements` MUST be `Setups.SetupSlot list` built with `EmptySlotContent`, and `git grep -n -w "TestElement" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing, every drawn, laid-out and run value unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the table's elements are slots: each one placed is empty, and each lays out as the table lays it out`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
